Text typed into an empty paragraph, or into new bold or italic, shows once after the admin's next update, on every frontend. The bridge used to put the caret in a text node the frontend never rendered (and replayed buffered keys into new nodes of its own, deleting the frontend's), so a frontend that keeps its DOM between renders — React, Vue, Next.js — drew the text again beside it. The bridge now hands the renderer a zero-width space in any empty element of a field it is drawing (never stored), so the node typed into is the frontend's own, and it types into that node.
